{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls","id":1138490,"title":"Idea: Coil of owls.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-07T21:22:53-07:00","id":1138490,"title":"Idea: Coil of owls.","content":"a rough idea just had for a coil trying to mimic the strix.<br /> <br /> 2 ways I see to do it.<br /> <br /> one is to just gairi like drea powers.<br /> <br /> other, is to allow <i>somewhat </i>safer posession.<br /> <br /> which do you think is better?<br /> <br /> note that a Dragon who failed the opposed roll would probaly be really, and truly screwed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T17:44:41-07:00","id":1138756,"title":"","content":"Ideas?<br /> Those who study this heretical Coil believe that the Birds of Dis represent the next evolutionary step beyond Vampirism. Adherents strive to shed their physical shells and become closer in mind, body, and deed to the malevolent entities known as the Strix. Some have even attained a measure of success while others fall rapidly to their Beasts or are rumored to suffer fates far worse than this.<br /> Unsurprisingly many students of this Coil attempt to keep their pursuits hidden, as Kindred society in general is unlikely to hold favorable views of their own kind emulating an entity that is so effectively... antagonistic towards the Kindred.<br /> <br /> It could make a great NPC plot line but the right kind of game could make it work with PCs too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T05:28:41-07:00","id":1139148,"title":"","content":"<u>Character ideas:</u><br /> <br /> <b>The Mad</b> (\u2013 or is it?) \u2013 Who believes the Owls are the purest form of existence. He is ever closer to the Draugr state, but we won\u2019t see it. He is so close to be free from this debased state, so close now\u2026<br /> <b>The Desperate</b> \u2013 He knows they are coming. He knows they will destroy every Kindred in the domain. He cannot run fast enough, so the only answer is\u2026 through?<br /> <b>The Mystic </b>\u2013 Owls are inmune to fire, hunger and sunlight: they are masters of their needs, not the other way around. They are the alfa and the omega, the Door that Which will Open in Darkness, the Undoing.<br /> <br /> <u>Imaginery:</u><br /> <br /> A hollowed vampire, his skin so thin that shifts and hangs from places it should not, the distinct shape of an Owl creature clearly flowing under it with each movement. After finishing the ritual, it falls on its knees, and opening his mouth to the sky he lets a piercing shriek that carries with it all the darkness that it has become. His former body collapses on the ground, empty as a shock puppet. Night wings fade in the forest shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T15:47:35-07:00","id":1139290,"title":"","content":"Think the emulating the Strix, or allowing <i>somewhat</i> safer possesion, is better?<br /> <br /> Tenatively thinking that the first is better use the safer possesion thing as a scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T15:57:18-07:00","id":1139294,"title":"","content":"&quot;Somewhat safer possession&quot; is a terrible idea. I don't mean terrible for the OP to have thought it up, I mean it's a terrible idea for whatever Dragon is harebrained enough to attempt it - which means <i>of course</i> someone will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T16:10:20-07:00","id":1139297,"title":"","content":"I agree, a failed roll... I shudder to think of what the Strix would do, to a Dragon wanting to keep them imprisoned within as a &quot;battery&quot;<br /> <br /> Thoughts on it working best as a scale?<br /> <br /> think a failure in such an attempt would make a good story arc?<br /> <br /> or even a sucess, and the local strix wanting to &quot;Avenge this insult&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-10-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T09:00:22-07:00","id":1139458,"title":"","content":"I think you need two paths: one that seeks to emulate the Strix and thereby shed the weaknesses of the vampiric form and nature. (&quot;Oh! Such purity in malevolence! Such adamantine strength before the Light! It mus be mine!&quot;)<br /> <br /> The other seeks to subsume the Strix, consuming them to create either a symbiotic relationship or a form of the ultimate predator--the True Apex. After all, the existence of the Strix gives lie to the idea that vampires are apex predators over man... predators, yes, but only another step toward... something?<br /> <br /> Anyway, this train of investigation is interesting as I have an NPC that might be entangled with the Strix in some fashion or other like this. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T09:23:54-07:00","id":1139468,"title":"","content":"I personally like the &quot;trying to mimic the Strix&quot; idea better.<br /> <br /> Mostly because Strix aren't common enough to learn how to resist their possession, and the first vampire that tried likely wouldn't survive long enough to finish.<br /> <br /> The first option is still useful even if there aren't any Strix around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T11:25:35-07:00","id":1139494,"title":"","content":"I'll note this whole concept is heretical for Ordo Dracul practices because of the prohibition against seeking infernal help because by vampire standard's Strix are pretty demonic.<br /> <br /> That said some vampire somewhere is going to be win the Darwin Award <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FateWorseThanDeath\" target=\"_blank\">or worse</a>.<br /> <br /> The Coil for this concept is a bit difficult. I think it make be better to make a collection of scales that represent testing on Strix victims.<br /> <br /> One idea is to use a Vitae-infused corpse (not Revenant nor Kindred) <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TailorMadePrison\" target=\"_blank\">as a Strix trap</a>, possibly by using acupuncture needles through Chakra, allow the Owl to be starved to oblivion or <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SealedEvilInACan\" target=\"_blank\">negotiated with.</a><br /> <br /> Another could be experiments on Ghosts produced via <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0245674/\" target=\"_blank\">certain types of death</a> and mystically manipulated Vitae to <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OutsideContextProblem\" target=\"_blank\">produce a Ghost that devour Strix</a>.<br /> <br /> Yet another idea could be a scale the result of experiments on stolen Reliquaries from the Lance that has some <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SwordOfPlotAdvancement\" target=\"_blank\">weapon</a> against the Strix.<br /> <br /> Or experiments that cause the vampire's body to be toxic to the strix, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ExploitedImmunity\" target=\"_blank\">possible via use of the weaknesses Strix have which the vampire doesn't.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1139468#post1139468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally like the &quot;trying to mimic the Strix&quot; idea better.<br /> <br /> Mostly because Strix aren't common enough to learn how to resist their possession, and the first vampire that tried likely wouldn't survive long enough to finish.<br /> <br /> The first option is still useful even if there aren't any Strix around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree if you want an actual Owl Coil this would be the way to go, with the above as possible Scales of that coil.<br /> <br /> What are the Strix's abilities that would be emulated and how would they fit together in a coil format are the next questions.<br /> <br /> Appearing as if you're already Strix possessed seems like a good base ability, as triggering the Loner Bane and seeming as not a valid target for possession (because it appears someone else is already home, so to speak) are handy and not too overpowered. Also flashing yellow eyes at vampires is a good way to scare them or get them to kill you. -bluff- Go ahead strike me down, but if you do I'll be wearing you as my next meat-suit, or we can negotiate, your choice... -bluff-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-11-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T13:39:38-07:00","id":1139537,"title":"","content":"So idea ? send false messages as first coil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T14:21:28-07:00","id":1139548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1139537#post1139537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So idea ? send false messages as first coil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A &quot;false&quot; Strix presence possibly the with effect of Owl Eyes to go with it, (After all the yellow eye are the major sign of the Strix, and some would say &quot;partial&quot; instead of &quot;false&quot;, if they knew the end result of walking the Coils of this particular Ouroboros) the Taint of Life being a good candidate for the Second Coil, possibly doing the Gathering Cry as the third coil.<br /> <br /> Depending on the metaphysics of your setting is where coils 4 and 5 get interesting, I'd have vampires shed their Personal, Clan, and Bloodline Banes at Coil 4 and would instead have them Gain Uncommon Banes as Strix do based on their Blood Potency which shall translate to Shadow Potency if they progress further. Mastering the 5th Coil means shedding Humanity, Mask and Dirge completely in exchange for a Vice as they become a Strix possessing their original body, thus meaning the destruction of that body doesn't mean their Final Death and basically be transformed into a Strix for Common Banes as well. They should also gain traits appropriate to their Strix-hood, like Dread Powers (Be sure to account for their Disciplines with Dread Powers slots) and shed non-Strix Vampire Traits. Note they should gain the benefit of <i>Embracing Embodiments</i> on page 201 for their Original Body if they don't have a high enough Shadow Potency to Possess themselves.<br /> <br /> How would I have a vampire learn this Coil?<br /> <br /> One possibility is a special ritualized Diablerizing of Revenants that have been possessed by Strix after the proper meditative study to harness and shape the forces. Why Revenants? Because their Vitae doesn't have the overpowering influence of a Clan and thus the residue left by the Strix's presence can be isolated and harvested. The game design reason being Revenants bring more chaos into the research because they can not be reliably made, as opposed to Kindred. More chaos in the research, more opportunity for story-hooks...<br /> <br /> By the way as I describe the Coil, the resulting Strix wouldn't actually have the Coil, the Coil itself being a marker of the Kindred's evolution along the path of becoming a Strix.<br /> <br /> One last parting thought: A Strix that comes into existence already with a body, oh how envious shall the other Strix be...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-11-2017, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T16:36:01-07:00","id":1139576,"title":"","content":"Becoming a Strix possesing the original body, seems, wrong for the 5th coil, as while they may study the Strix, and seek to emulate them in some ways, it doesnt follow that they seek to emulate them in all ways.<br /> <br /> I do agree the coil would be considered VERY Heretical<br /> <br /> Idealology aside it would be prosecuted more harshly then the Coil of Ziva<br /> <br /> because, it could draw the attention of the Strix to the vampire doing the research<br /> <br /> not something I think any remotely sane vampire wants.<br /> <br /> Ziva can be looked the other way to, if a handful of followers achieve the princes Recognition, they might become part of the core group of some domains local Ordo Dracul Covenant, if thats what the ST wants to do.<br /> <br /> I doubt the coil of owls will be able to do that as the prince would also censure them, the Circle and Sanctum alike would decrie it as blasphemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-11-2017, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T10:10:28-07:00","id":1139724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1139576#post1139576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming a Strix possessing the original body, seems, wrong for the 5th coil... -snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it seems <i>wrong </i>because it is a cheat; In a mere five coils it objectively reaches a stated goal of the Ordo Dracul which is to transcend the vampiric state. Strix are in a meaningful sense vampiric gods (little 'g'); they are immortal in ways that put even vampires to shame, they are the boogieman of kindred, the weakest of which can still terrify even the most powerful kindred, they lack the struggle to remain sapient which is represented by Humanity, and are free to do <i>anything </i>they want without fear of guilt or conscious. Because they are out of context problems for the other splats and can easily just leave if they even suspect something that could adversely affect them, they are <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DarkIsEvil\" target=\"_blank\">spooky shadowy figures</a> that can cause damage and leave to cause horror to their <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MadeOfEvil\" target=\"_blank\">wicked shadowy heart's</a> delight.<br /> <br /> Given the reward, the risks are not unreasonable. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryA8PafooQ4\" target=\"_blank\">It is completely sane to want to be a Strix, it's just morally reprehensible</a><br /> <br /> The main downside of being a Strix is the lack of a body for all of its sensations, and if you start with a body and work to make sure you can get others later, that isn't much of a downside, and in fact being assured of continued existence past your corporeal existence in a way that can still affect and interact with the world is a serious upside.<br /> <br /> I'd say there would be a whole slew of vampires eager to become Strix if they were sure their identities would remains intact and it wasn't difficult, and that makes this whole thing devastating to the setting unless it'd be really difficult and then it'd be hated and feared because a peer you've been in petty squabbles with or childer you've mistreated could become capable of turning into a monster several orders of magnitudes worse than you.<br /> <br /> Actually with how wonderfully tempting this is I'd possibly up the ante of the requirements, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1139548#post1139548\">ritualized diablerizing of Revenants</a> which were previously possessed by a Strix <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PoweredByAForsakenChild\" target=\"_blank\">whom were new born</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EatsBabies\" target=\"_blank\">infant</a> that are <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0099710/\" target=\"_blank\">more than two lunar months past birth but less than three lunar months old</a>. That steepens the curve of the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MoralEventHorizon\" target=\"_blank\">moral event horizon</a> and makes such a thing specifically difficult to obtain to the point it'd pretty much need to be arranged. The in game metaphysics as to why? The blood of the infant's mother would have been replaced by the infant's blood at that point and still have not developed to much interference from life experience tainting the vessel, and only the vessels <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ChildrenAreInnocent\" target=\"_blank\">own pure innocent </a>blood can since it properly. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/IfYoureSoEvilEatThisKitten\" target=\"_blank\">Also if you're going to be a being of evil and darkness this is a way to initiate yourself into being total evil.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>All that said:</b> What I am suggesting is not a &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GottaCatchThemAll\" target=\"_blank\">neat new power</a>&quot;, I am suggesting something that is <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AppliedPhlebotinum\" target=\"_blank\">Applied Phlebotinum</a> designed to power the plot devices of a whole Chronicle, like a nuclear reactor powering a whole city, not a gas-generator you can haul in your truck.<br /> <br /> <b>Alternate idea: </b>Have a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DarkIsNotEvil\" target=\"_blank\">Tengu </a>variant that uses these tropes: <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EmbodimentOfVirtue\" target=\"_blank\">Embodiment of Virtue</a>, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeroicWillpower\" target=\"_blank\">Heroic Will</a>, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ThanatosGambit\" target=\"_blank\">Thanatos Gambit</a>, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ObiWanMoment\" target=\"_blank\">Obi Wan Moment</a>, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DeathActivatedSuperpower\" target=\"_blank\">Death-Activated Superpowers</a><br /> <br /> Then have the Tengu fighting the Strix! In fact you could have the Tengu be the result of an ancient Covenant with meditative moral-based quasi-Ordo <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_elements_(Japanese_philosophy)\" target=\"_blank\">Eastern Alchemical </a>practices/beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-12-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T13:11:45-07:00","id":1139754,"title":"","content":"And because a Dragon wants to emulate the Strixes power, doesnt mean he's allied with them, working with or for them, or worships them, and doesnt preclude working against them. just noting &quot;Hey they have 2 or 3 advantages we dont and are so close to us... so... lets bridge the gap a bit&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T13:52:02-07:00","id":1139762,"title":"","content":"00<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1139754#post1139754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And because a Dragon wants to emulate the Strixes power, doesn't mean he's allied with them, working with or for them, or worships them, and doesn't preclude working against them. just noting &quot;Hey they have 2 or 3 advantages we dont and are so close to us... so... lets bridge the gap a bit&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, and also very true among Strix themselves. I'll cite the Loner Uncommon Bane and the Strix-Hunter as VtR 2nd Ed as prime examples.<br /> <br /> For the Alternate Idea Tengu <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/GoodIsNotSoft\" target=\"_blank\">are no less monsters from the kindred perspective</a>, perhaps more so because somehow they seem to have <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AbominationAccusationAttack\" target=\"_blank\">moral high groun</a>d against the kindred, as opposed to the Strix. I mean Kindred are monsters after all and possessing them and stopping them from causing harm is virtuous, so yeah, I'd expect kindred to be frightened of tengu for <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HunterOfMonsters\" target=\"_blank\">different reasons</a> than strix.<br /> <br /> Also the Tengu idea could have a path where they sacrifice Humanity in particularly virtuous ways, becoming <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HolyIsNotSafe\" target=\"_blank\">more frighteningly moral</a> than human.<br /> <br /> In fact, Tengu could 100% explain <i>VII</i>. There is a scary thought...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Questions: </b><br /> Is your intent to make a power set balanced with the rest of the game that can be reasonable collected without overturning the setting?<br /> Alternatively are you you looking to craft something to power plot devices which drive stories forward because they are outside the normal spectrum of power/scope?<br /> <br /> I'll note Strix are written in a way Idigam for Forsaken are written, as problems that defy all the humdrum normal solutions within reach of characters within the setting, forcing conflict outside the setting standard. Vampire is more about paranoia so vampire possessing boogieman make sense for that role, Forsaken is about spiritual knowledge/combat savagery/maintaining ecosystems and Idigam are Godzilla scale combat foes and strange unknown powers outside normal spirit knowledge, fundamentally shaking spirit ecosystems/economies in their wake. The nature of the Strix is why my suggestion presume the second question is yes and not the first, but knowing your intent would let tailor my suggestions better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-12-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T09:01:31-07:00","id":1139947,"title":"","content":"I'd like only to chime in and applaud the focus on tropes, and calling out the specific tropes used, as a foil for the Storyteller to wield. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3279_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3279\" data-vbnamecard=\"3279\">Pale_Crusader</a> tho art the wind beneath our (one) wing. <br /> <br /> Back to the topic at hand: keep in mind that not all coils went to 5 originally (1e, I think), so the final dot of this one may not have even been discovered yet. That could make it both a plot point (one or several individuals are working toward it) and also more palatable for use by a PC. You could, also, make the 5th dot somewhat less... complete... and instead make the transformation ritual into a scale that requires 5 dots (among other things). That also highlights the extra effort required to cross the threshold into darkness and smoke....<br /> <br /> This approach could in particular work well if you wanted to branch the coil and call out its ability to transform vampires into either Strix or Tengu--the later being an inversion of the logic that led to full application of the Coil.<br /> <br /> If a coil-like path is how you get Tengu, then linking them to VII is also interesting. Your mind is an enjoyable place, good gentle! <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T02:37:46-07:00","id":1140462,"title":"","content":"Ok, let me try. Feedback appreciated.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Coil of Shadows</span></b></span><br /> The Coil of Shadow is a set of self-hypnosis techniques and mediation on the nature of evil, made for the Dragon to avoid the trapping of Humanity and embracing his dark side. Becoming a true monster himself, his Beast catch up in malevolence, becoming something unexpected.<br /> <b>0 Detachment</b><br /> The first step for achieving pure evil is to eshew his human ties to the world. The Vampire loose all his Touchstones, and cannot bind new ones (unless forfeiting the Coil, loosing all spent experiences). He suffer normal penalty to detachment rolls for not having Touchstones, but is immune to the Languid condition.<br /> <b>00 Malevolent Intent</b><br /> The Vampire mold his mindset into one single wicked focus, loosing his Mask and Dirge to gain a Vice, similar to the Vice of a Strix. He can as a reflexive action convert 2 Vitae into a Willpower. He cannot gain Willpower any other way than through Vice or Vitae. As a strange side effect, he can now hear a Strix's Gathering Cry, and understand what it is.<br /> <b>000 Shadow Beast</b><br /> The Vampire's Beast change into something sinister. When he enter Frenzy, he completly loose control of himself and cannot spend willpower to act against its Beast. He cannot remember anything that happen during it, and doesn't have to roll for detachment unless he discover what he has done after the Frenzy. Whatever the initial stimulus of the Frenzy, the goal of the Beast is always to indulge the Vampire's Vice. The Vampire doesn't appear to be in Frenzy, and may act as patient and composed as he would normally be. During the Frenzy, he is considered as being possessed by a Strix with no Dread Powers.<br /> <b>0000 Infinite Hunger</b><br /> Amaranth is the ultimate sin for a Kindred, and the character reveal in it. He is now able to diablerize Mortals, with the only benefit of gaining Skills. Mortals resist Diablerie with their Integrity instead of Blood Potency. He can also diablerize Strix in material form (possessing a host or using the Materialize Embodiement) to gain Dread Powers (except for Kindred Discipline, which are diablerized normally). These Dread Powers are only available during Frenzy, or if the Vampire has achieved the fifth level of this Coil. He gains Tainted as a permanent Condition.<br /> <b>00000 Inhuman Monster</b><br /> The Vampire achieve what he believe is its ultimate goal, and loose his Humanity. It is replaced for all intent by (10 - Blood Potency), including for mortal interaction. He is considered a Draugr for any power that can gauge Humanity. He is now identical to Strix in Synthesis, with only the Dread Powers he has acquired with the previous level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","user":"Nepher","date":".  Added Integrity resistance for mortals in level 4 09-15-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T05:59:25-07:00","id":1140496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140462#post1140462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">0000 Infinite Hunger<br /> Amaranth is the ultimate sin for a Kindred, and the character reveal in it. He is now able to Diablerize Mortals, with the only benefit of gaining Skills. He can also Diablerize Strix in material form (possessing a host or using the Materialize Embodiement) to gain Dread Powers (except for Kindred Discipline, which are Diablerized normally). These Dread Powers are only available during Frenzy, or if the Vampire has achieved the fifth level of this Coil. He gains Tainted as a permanent Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like most of what you did, but vampires are already capable of diablerizing mortals, and they get skill dots from it. It was brought up in 1000 years of night, and I believe there might've been a humanity level prerequisite. So maybe make it so that the humanity level prerequisite need not apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T06:19:01-07:00","id":1140502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140496#post1140496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like most of what you did, but vampires are already capable of diablerizing mortals, and they get skill dots from it. It was brought up in 1000 years of night, and I believe there might've been a humanity level prerequisite. So maybe make it so that the humanity level prerequisite need not apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about that, but it's for Elder with Humanity 6+ only. For most Vampire, it's not possible. Let say it's another way to achieve it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But thank you for pointing it, I have a minor change to make to match TTYN rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","user":"Nepher","date":". 09-15-2017, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T08:33:39-07:00","id":1140522,"title":"","content":"Edit: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LTRTPPS4Mqt6Kl6eOo7C4HDJzL475F_WCcgEhn_ow_Q/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Here's</a> the updated version of the Coil, including the Scales.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Coil of Smoke</b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Unholy Visage \u2022</i></span><br /> Similar to the Blush of Health, the vampire may use one Vitae to bring something to the surface for the duration of a scene. In this case it's the Beast and it's similarities to the Strix. Eyes gleam yellow and her aura is stained by diablerie until the effect wears off. Non-corporeal forms, such as Primeval Miasma, may also exhibit other traits such as the outlines of wings or an owl's head. Additionally, any supernatural powers that can detect whether someone is a vampire or a Strix will face a Clash of Wills. Failure means the vampire registers as a Strix.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Omen Sensitivity \u2022\u2022</i></span><br /> The Birds of Dis are rarely seen outside of disaster areas, potential or actual. The reason for this is their innate sense of impending chaos and destruction. Now this sense is the dragon's, allowing him to sense any potential disasters within Blood Potency months before they happen. Any fortune, fate or luck altering powers or Merits in the immediate vicinity of the Dragon will also trigger this sense. In either case the sensation is vague, only indicating when the disaster will strike or who's the subject of the power. It does not alert the dragon as to what the disaster might be or what the power actually does.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Summon the Parliament \u2022\u2022\u2022</i></span><br /> One of the lesser known tricks of the Birds of Dis is their ability to call out for each other. This Coil allows the dragon to hear this call as if she was a Strix herself. More importantly, when Unholy Visage is activated the vampire is capable of spending a point of Willpower and use the Gathering Cry herself. The call is heard a number of miles equal to the vampire's Stamina + Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Breath-Drinking \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i></span><br /> One of the few well known tricks of the Strix is their ability to steal life straight out of the mouth of their victims. This ability is now the dragon\u2019s. While in a grapple she can use a modified form of the Feed move that doesn\u2019t require biting the victim. This procedure is far from the euphoric experience of the Kiss, and conscious victims always get the Scarred Condition, if applicable. The move cannot be used on vampires, whose Vitae is too tightly bound in their blood, or on victims suffering Soulloss who aren\u2019t producing any Vitae at all, but it\u2019s theorized that it\u2019s possible to steal Vitae from Strix by using this method.<br /> Vitae gained through Breath Drinking are marked as Shadow Vitae on the sheet. Such Vitae can be used to fuel most of the vampire\u2019s repertoire, with the exceptions of Discipline activations that requires spilling Vitae in the form of blood, and the Blush of Life. The dragon can store a combined total of Vitae and Shadow Vitae equal to their maximum Vitae pool<span style=\"color:#A9A9A9\">, but can\u2019t store more Shadow Vitae than their unmodified maximum Vitae pool. The extra Vitae storage gained from Coil of Blood can\u2019t be used to store Shadow Vitae</span>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Shadow Mastery \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</i></span><br /> The power allows the dragon to purchase the Strix\u2019 Dread Powers, which can only be powered by Shadow Vitae stolen through Breath-Drinking.<br /> Make sure your Storyteller allows the chosen Dread Power, and substitute all activations dice pools with a relevant Attribute + Skill dice pool decided at the time of purchase. Any references to Shadow Potency are replaced with Blood Potency, which includes the prerequisites for each power, and the cost for each individual Dread Power is 4 Experiences, same as Out-of-Clan Disciplines. Kindred Disciplines are specifically not allowed.<br /> <br /> Edit: I coloured a section of text refering to our homebrewed version of Coil of Blood so you know to ignore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-30-2018, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T03:39:28-07:00","id":1141356,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>Sample Scales of Smoke</b></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Clipping the Darkened Wing</i></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coils:</b> Summon the Parliament<br /> <b>Procedure:</b> The subject has to be a vessel with a Vitae pool, such as a vampire or a ghoul. The dragon prepares a mixture using one point of Vitae and various esoteric oils. The resulting solution is then injected into the subject.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The subject gains one Vitae, along with the risk of the blood bond. This specific Vitae is tracked separately on the character sheet. If the subject becomes possessed by a Strix while not having used up this Vitae, the Strix becomes trapped. Only through winning an opposed Shadow Potency roll against the Vitae donor\u2019s Blood Potency can the Strix end the possession. The Strix can only attempt dispossession once every 24 hours and, unlike an unpossessed vessel, can\u2019t use up the marked Vitae.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Donning the Formless Shroud</i></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coils:</b> Breath-Drinking<br /> <b>Procedure:</b> Lorem ipsum.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The subject gains the Shadow Form of the Strix. She gains the three simplified Attributes Power, Finesse and Resistance, which is equal to her original Intelligence, Wits and Resolve respectively. She also gains Size according to the Shadow Potency table (p. 201), and updates her derived traits according to the rules of Strix. While in this form she does not gain access to her normal, blood-bound Vitae. Instead, all of her vampiric abilities needs to be powered by Shadow Vitae, as described above.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Consume the Shadow</i></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coils:</b> Shadow Mastery<br /> <b>Procedure:</b> Lorem ipsum.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Unknown.<br /> No cases of performing this Scale has been documented, but the theorized outcome by the Scale\u2019s late creator was the successful diablerie of a Strix, gaining Blood Experience equal to the Strix\u2019 Shadow Potency, as well as gaining one new Dread Power that the Strix knew. If this is possible it would undoubtedly be a Breaking Point on par with diablerizing a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I know that I haven't written two of the procedures, but I'm just not getting any inspiration for them. Any suggestions (or other kinds of feedback) are very welcome.<br /> <br /> Speaking of feedback:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140462#post1140462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, let me try. Feedback appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the first two dots. They're messing with the vampire template in ways that are unexpected but not broken. I might use versions of those two dots for another hypothetical Coil of mine about messing with the concept of Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a hre